From the vendor sensor-module mode records and the upstream S5KJN1 driver.

This teaches drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c the board's 19.2 MHz MCLK and adds
the four vendor mode tables for it.  The driver now selects its mode set from
the MCLK rate the camera clock actually provides, so a mode can never be
programmed with PLL values computed for another clock: the 24 MHz set is the
upstream one, the 19.2 MHz set is the vendor's.

The vendor mode tables are generated data.  They are the byte-for-byte
register writes of com.qti.sensormodule.liuqin_qtech_s5kjn1_wide_i.bin
(regSetting records 41/904/1767/2630), extracted from the parsed containers
in liuqin-mainline-blobs/camera/ during bring-up.  Vendor write order is
preserved; the vendor delay fields, which are all zero in these four records,
are not representable in struct cci_reg_sequence.

Frame rates at the unchanged 700 MHz link (560 Mpix/s, 4 lanes, 10 bit) are
10.07/30.06/30.06/60.12 fps for 8160x6120, 4080x3060, 4080x2296 and
3840x2160.

Bring-up assumptions kept explicit: the mode exposure defaults and exposure
margins are not part of the vendor records (the driver needs a value and the
sensor's minimum vertical blanking is unknown), so they are conservative
one-line-of-black defaults.

